# Python build artifacts
#   __pycache__/, *.py[cod]  bytecode, rewritten on every import
#   *.egg-info/              metadata generated by `pip install -e .`
# All three are derived from the tracked sources and never edited by hand.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Local environment and tool caches
#   .venv/          the virtualenv itself
#   .pytest_cache/  pytest's last-run state
# Machine-specific, and .venv/ is multi-GB: it holds a torch build pinned to
# this host's CUDA driver version, so it would not even work on another
# machine (see ROLLBACK_TORCH.md).
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Training run outputs
#   runs/   one directory per experiment: resolved_config.json + checkpoints
#   *.pt    checkpoints written anywhere outside runs/
#   logs/   per-epoch stdout from overhear_uplink.train
# Tens of MB per run, and fully reproducible from the tracked configs/ via
# launch_gpu_sweep.sh. The recipe is versioned; the weights it produces are not.
runs/
*.pt
logs/

# Evaluation stderr
# results/ is otherwise tracked on purpose — it holds the measurements the
# study reports. Only captured stderr is dropped: warning noise, no numbers.
results/*.err
